<!--
  Every piece of user-facing text in the app, in one place. Android strongly
  encourages this instead of writing text directly in layout XML or Kotlin code,
  for two big reasons: (1) it makes translating the app into other languages
  just a matter of adding a values-XX/strings.xml with the same names but
  different text, and (2) it means changing wording never requires touching
  code. Referenced from XML as "@string/app_title" and from Kotlin as
  R.string.app_title (or context.getString(R.string.app_title) when you need
  the actual text, not just a reference to it).
-->
